  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds a reproducible, exact screen for one seven-term E6 decoder mechanism: a one-extra rank-one extension of the six-term Gram factorization, with the dense pairing `B0` fixed. Across the 36 projective E6 root directions, all 364 projective `{-1,0,1}^6` directions in the pinned basis, and all rational lambda support cells, the minimum raw and fully charged Theorem C costs are both 40. This family therefore misses the requested cost-35 target. The result is scoped to this factorization and finite direction alphabet; it does not settle arbitrary seven-term E6 decoders and makes no kappa claim.\n\nThe package includes the exact identity, root/basis reconstruction, breakpoint coverage argument, cost certificate, positive fixtures, and negative controls. It preserves the initial root-only screen (566 cells, minimum 42) and records the one bounded pivot to the ternary directions.\n\n## Pins and reproduction\n\n- Exact base: `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`\n- Cycle 30 seed: `4dd9ff38bfc63aa200c17c947da92d9e`; track `complex-mechanisms`\n- Package: `research/e6-one-extra-frame-seed4dd9/`\n- Reproduce: `python3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/e6-one-extra-frame-seed4dd9`\n\nChecks completed locally:\n- Package metadata and source pins pass.\n- Exact package verifier passes normally and under `python3 -O` on Python 3.14.7.\n- The predecessor's focused E6 exact baseline check passes, confirming the six-term reference ranks `(6,7,6,6,6,6)` and cost 37.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n\nThe registered replay hook is configured for Python 3.12, which is not installed in this environment; its wrapper reports that requirement. The declared verifier itself was run directly under the available Python 3.14.7. CI replay remains useful for the configured runtime.\n\n## Scope and credit\n\nThis differs from the rank-four E6 screens in PRs #2137 and #2232: it uses seven terms and a redundant rank-one frame, holding `G` and `B0` fixed. It builds on merged PR #1590's root-unit model and Theorem C pricing; open PR #2228 separately leaves overcomplete E6 at seven terms open. No physical supplier mapping, changed paid profile, selected-frontier change, or independent human review is claimed. Prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex GPT-6 assistance.\n",
